1:# Context: why the ASDEX SOL run crashes with a Dirichlet phi BC at the inner radial boundary
2-
3-Written 2026-10-02 to resume a debugging conversation (1–2 Oct 2026). All findings come from
4-analysing existing output and reading the Gkeyll source; no simulation was rerun by the assistant.
5-
6-## The question
7-
8:An ASDEX-Upgrade SOL simulation (Gkeyll gyrokinetic app, 2x2v, p=1, input `ASDEX_no_impurities.c`)
9-crashes when the potential has a homogeneous Dirichlet BC (`phi = 0`) at the inner radial (x-lower)
10-boundary, and survives with homogeneous Neumann there. Is that an input error or a Gkeyll bug?
11-
--
80-essentially no ions (200 V run, upper plate, first cell: electron flux −5e22 to −1.4e23, ion flux → 0).
81-
82-Code reading that explains this:
83:- `gk_collisionless_flux_edge_surfy_2x2v_ser_p1.c`: the z-edge flux upwinds between ghost and skin using
84-  the sign of the full phase-space speed (parallel + curvature + ExB). There is no special case for the
85-  sheath BC (only `GKYL_BC_GK_SKIP` selects different kernels).
86-- `bc_sheath_gyrokinetic.c` and its kernels: the ghost is the skin distribution mirrored in `vpar` below


